      "updated": 1795546955703,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "* argparse.Namespace: is a lightweight, empty\ncontainer object returned by `parser.parse_args()`\nwhose sole purpose is to store your parsed CLI\narguments as attributes.\n\n* What it is: A minimal Python class wrapping a\nstandard dictionary (`__dict__`) that maps resolved\nargument names (strings) to references of their\nparsed values (`int`, `str`, `bool`, `None`, etc.).\n\n* Why it exists: To let you access parsed inputs\ncleanly via dot notation (`args.count`) instead of\ndictionary bracket syntax (`args[\"count\"]`), without\nbundling any parsing logic inside the data itself.\n\n **Key behaviors:**\n* Every registered `.add_argument()` becomes a\nguaranteed attribute on it (holding its parsed\nvalue, `default`, or `None`).\n\n* `vars(args)` extracts its underlying `dict`\ndirectly.\n\n* `print(args)` outputs a readable summary like\n`Namespace(name='Alice', count=3)`.",
      "fontSize": 12.910073916418993,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "* argparse.Namespace: is a lightweight, empty container object returned by `parser.parse_args()` whose sole purpose is to store your parsed CLI arguments as attributes.\n\n* What it is: A minimal Python class wrapping a standard dictionary (`__dict__`) that maps resolved argument names (strings) to references of their parsed values (`int`, `str`, `bool`, `None`, etc.).\n\n* Why it exists: To let you access parsed inputs cleanly via dot notation (`args.count`) instead of dictionary bracket syntax (`args[\"count\"]`), without bundling any parsing logic inside the data itself.\n\n **Key behaviors:**\n* Every registered `.add_argument()` becomes a guaranteed attribute on it (holding its parsed value, `default`, or `None`).\n\n* `vars(args)` extracts its underlying `dict` directly.\n\n* `print(args)` outputs a readable summary like `Namespace(name='Alice', count=3)`.",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
